# Code quality gate (unitor-win64-driver)

Short guidance. **Numbers are enforced by the analyser**, not by an agent redesign loop.

## Principles

- **KISS** — simplest design that meets the current need.
- **YAGNI** — only what the story requires; no hooks “for later”.
- **WET → DRY** — duplicating once is OK; factorize when the pattern is stable (~2nd–3rd time).
- **Boy Scout (scoped)** — improve the zone changed for the ticket; do **not** clean an entire large file because one line moved.
- **English everywhere** in code and comments.
- **Naming** — camelCase locals/methods; PascalCase types; `kPascalCase` constants; instance members `name_`. Names must reveal intent.
- **Names over narrative comments** — rename or extract instead of narrating *what*; comments only for *why* / non-obvious constraints (including dated MIDI/USB timing exceptions).

## Thresholds (source of truth = analyser)

| Metric | Max |
|---|---|
| Function (protocol / core) | ~40 lines |
| Function (USB / platform glue) | ~50 lines |
| Parameters (our code) | 4 |
| Cyclomatic complexity | 10 (glue up to 12 if justified) |
| Nesting depth | 4 |
| Useful `.cpp` file | ~400 lines |

Win32 / third-party APIs are not rewritten to satisfy parameter counts. Historical debt outside the diff is a separate chore.

## Hot MIDI / USB path

In transfer callbacks and encode/decode loops on the latency-sensitive path: no unbounded alloc, no dangerous locks, no logging that risks jitter. **Safety wins** over metrics — document a dated `NOLINT` / exception rather than obscure the critical path.

## Definition of done

1. Project compiles (when a target exists).
2. Relevant tests pass (when they exist).
3. `python scripts/quality/lint-touched.py` passes on touched C++ under gate scopes.

If the analyser fails → fix the finding. **No** mandatory DESIGN → AUTO-REVIEW redesign loop.
